    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53">

                <pb facs="0326" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg40"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2801</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-14T18:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 15, 6 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>688. I believe it is now thought Germany will not declare war and that Italy may
                    feel compelled to take the initiative before long, as her allies are urging
                    it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
